Read `AGENTS.md` at the repo root first, every session. It is the ONE agent instruction file
for this repo (Claude Code, Cursor, Replit, any other tool) — operating contract, mandatory
read order, git-flow rules, the two-tier work-claim model (GitHub Issues for durable task
ownership, `WORK/LOCK.md` for short-lived file-edit locks), gates, and PR flow.

Do not duplicate its content here. This file is only a pointer so Cursor bootstraps from the
same source of truth as every other environment working this repo — if `AGENTS.md` changes,
follow the new version, not any assumption baked into this file.

Before editing code: read `AGENTS.md`, then `WORK/LOOP_STATE.md` and `WORK/FORWARD_PLAN.md`,
then `WORK/LOCK.md`. Work in an isolated worktree for anything you intend to commit
(`tools/new-worktree.sh <task-slug>`) — never a second clone. Never merge to `master`;
that requires Sri's explicit sign-off.
